hi i'm catherine mccord from welicious  and this is pro tips from pro chefs  [Music]  i'm going to show you some tsa approved  recipes that are so simple to make and  with these hacks and tips it's going to  make preparing these recipes a breeze  here's how to do it this is one of my  favorite recipes to make when i travel  because first of all it's only three  ingredients you're going to take a flour  tortilla about this size but if you have  something smaller or larger that's going  to work too you're going to take peanut  butter and then of course your banana so  start by taking your tortilla on a flat  surface and then you're just going to  take some good creamy peanut butter but  my kids they like a lot of peanut butter  so i give it a nice coating all across  and just spread spread spread you can  even go to the very edge right here  because you're going to be rolling it up  having a protein a fruit and a  carbohydrate really will save you for  hours and hours and of course like i  said it's tsa approved no one's going to  stop you unless of course someone wants  a bite so with a banana i always  recommend trying to find a straight  banana now finding a straight banana not  always easy but  i think we'll go with this one so  peel your banana and again you want to  make sure that you have a banana that's  nice and sweet so place it in the side  closest to you  and take the tortilla and press it with  the peanut butter and slowly rolling it  up  pushing the tortilla on all sides  against that banana and just keep  pulling it towards you and make tight  tight tight and then again you've got  that peanut butter right there that is  your glue  so just put it face down  and then you want a serrated knife and i  almost like to do this like sushi  this is like sushi you'll see when i  show you in the middle and then just  turn it like this so nice even sized  pieces and you can make them smaller or  larger i like to say about one inch  oh aren't they cute look at this  i just want you to see look at that  you've got that beautiful banana right  in the middle so sweet but you've also  got the like kind of saltiness from the  peanut butter now let's also talk about  containers because you want to make sure  that when you're traveling especially if  you're traveling with kids that you keep  them busy and you keep their bellies  full so that they don't have those like  sugar just crashes in the middle of the  flight no one needs that especially not  me so i like to use a bento box  container like this so a bento box  container like this is a huge help  because not only can you see all of your  choices but it's got a divider in the  middle but it's great because you can  just put these little banana dog bites  right in like this  so that they'll stay separated  nice and fresh and then you have it for  the flight to wherever you're going and  then whenever you get somewhere and  you're ready to fly back you can refill  it i've got strawberries and blueberries  i've got the banana dog bites you have  got a full complete meal right here and  super affordable too  [Music]  when you're traveling through tsa these  cookies are a mouthful of good for you  food the last thing i want are foods  that leave crumbs all over my seat  that's why these breakfast cookies are  like magic they have just this nice  little bit of chew so  no crumbs they're packed with protein  from pistachios and the flax seeds which  are also packed with omega-3 fatty acids  there's no refined sugar they're made  with applesauce and maple syrup and  they've got dried cherries and  pistachios but you could also just go  wild and add chocolate chips or any of  your other favorite nuts but they're  also great to just freeze and take with  you on the go  whenever i want to really impress my  kids especially when we're traveling i  make this blackberry tea cake it's  really sweet cuts beautifully into  squares and it has this like jewel that  you find in every single bite so here's  how to do it you're gonna butter and  flour your pan and then after it cools a  little bit you're gonna flip it out okay  i heard it flip so that's a good sign  and then  it's so much fun to make  and when you cut it  look at this  you get these like perfect little bites  of blackberry in every bite it's really  stable so that you can just cut it into  squares pack it in any kind of zipper  bags or foil carry it right on the plane  one of the best things about this  blackberry tea cake is it's not crumbly  you can just open a bite of it  and look at that  all these beautiful blackberries in  every bite and no mess when you're  traveling you better hope that your  neighbor sitting in the seat next to you  doesn't try to steal a bite  for more pro tips head to the  drewbarramoreshow.com  slash pro tips and if you make any of  these recipes tag me  licious hashtag drewbarrowmore show  this was so much fun i hope everybody  has a great time traveling thanks for  having me drew see you soon  [Music]
 

